# Session store isolation

Cursor and Claude are separate products with separate session files. A delete, wipe, hide, archive, or “leave no trace” request applies **only** to the product the user named.

## Stores

- **Cursor:** `composerHeaders`, `cursorDiskKV`, `composerData`, conversation-search, `~/.cursor/projects/**/agent-transcripts`, `~/.cursor/memory`, `glass.claudeCodeSessionRegistry.v1` visibility/archive flags that only change Cursor’s sidebar.
- **Claude:** `~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl`, `~/.claude_personal/**`, `~/.claude/session-env`, `~/.config/Claude/claude-code-sessions`, `~/.config/ClaudePersonal/claude-code-sessions`, `~/.local/share/cursor-to-claude-sync/exports.json`.

## Do not infer Claude from Cursor

These are **not** permission to write or delete Claude:

- same title (`[cursor] …`, `(1)`, import sibling)
- AgentMigration / `localComposerId` / registry association
- export ledger dest UUID
- “the other listing of this chat”
- “leave no trace” after a Cursor-only order
- “delete, not hide” when the hide was a Cursor archive flag

## Required wording

Delete or alter Claude files only when the user names Claude (or Claude Desktop / `~/.claude` / that CLI session id) in the same order.

If the user said Cursor and you think the Claude copy should go too, **stop and ask**. Do not archive Claude as a substitute for asking.

## Examples

```
# ❌ BAD — user: "Delete both [cursor] … chats on Cursor"
rm ~/.claude/projects/**/851e2e36-….jsonl
# also bad: delete Desktop indexes, Personal copies, or the export ledger row

# ✅ GOOD — Cursor rows/transcripts/search only. Leave Claude JSONL and indexes alone.
```
